    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭŏchīnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		Antiochus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of King Antiochus Magnus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 11, 7, 17</span></i>
			; cf. Fasti Capitol. Baiter, p. xli.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to the
				philosopher Antiochus</i>, <i>the founder of the
				fifth Academy</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 9, 8, 1</span></i>.</div>
